.TH "LIBPKGEXEC\-LINUX" "3" "" "libpkgexec\-linux" "Version 0.7.0"
.SH NAME
libpkgexec\-linux \- Linux execution backends for libpkgexec
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]#include <libpkgexec\-linux/libpkgexec\-linux.h>\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]libpkgexec\-linux\f[R] implements Linux backends for sealed \f[B]libpkgexec\f[R] requests.
.PP
\f[B]host_supervisor_backend\f[R] uses the current root and network views, current credentials, exact interpreter bytes, a closed environment, complete pipe capture, and verified process\-tree cleanup.
.PP
\f[B]isolated_backend\f[R] constructs a private mount namespace from one exact dedicated root\-view directory.
It clones that root read\-only, \f[B]nosuid\f[R], and \f[B]nodev\f[R], and attaches admitted read\-only or writable directory resources at their declared logical paths with \f[B]nodev\f[R].
The root must contain the interpreter and complete runtime closure.
The backend overlays a private execution\-only \f[I]/dev\f[R] containing deterministic \f[I]/dev/null\f[R] and imports no ambient host \f[I]/dev\f[R].
.PP
For \f[B]allowed\f[R] networking the isolated backend preserves the caller\[aq]s network namespace.
For \f[B]denied\f[R] networking it creates a private network namespace with only administratively down loopback.
For \f[B]loopback\-only\f[R] networking it creates the private namespace and brings up only loopback.
.PP
Both backends implement \f[B]controlled_execution_backend\f[R].
Disabled cancellation uses the ordinary execution call.
Graceful\-then\-forced cancellation requires the exact request\-bound token.
Where the end\-to\-end pidfd probe succeeds, the backend creates a private execution session, sends signals through pidfds, honors the sealed grace period, and verifies descendant cleanup.
.PP
Both backends require current credentials.
Where the realization probes succeed, they admit exact address\-space, file\-size, and open\-files limits and seal them against later mutation.
They provide no user or PID namespace, Landlock, cgroup, CPU\-time, or execution\-wide process\-count guarantee.
